  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nAn elevated heat risk will be the name of the game over the \nnext few days low level flow generally SW to W over the next \nseveral days. As a result, some weak WAA will allow low level \nthicknesses to increase closer to 1430m. Based off the offices \nclimatological study this is forecast to result in highs in the \nlow to mid 90s across the inland areas and upper 80s to low 90s \nalong the OBX and coast through much of the week before a front \nimpacts the region resulting in cooler temperatures late week \ninto the weekend. \n\nHeat indices are expected to peak around 100-110 each afternoon\nthrough Thurs, and potentially lingering into Fri with daily heat\nheadlines probable for much of the area. For today, have \nexpanded the Heat Advisory to include the Inner Banks, which \nleaves NW counties the the OBX out as they are expected to\nremain just below criteria. We encourage anyone planning on \nspending alot of time outdoors this week to take proper \nprecautions and stay hydrated.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nA typical summer time pattern will remain in place through much\nthe week with a series of shortwaves/MCS's moving through WNW \nflow aloft bringing periods of showers and thunderstorms across\nthe region. With a moist and unstable airmass in place, could \nsee daily seabreeze related storms developing each afternoon, \nhowever best forcing will occur as individual shortwaves move \nacross the region, which at this time appears to be late \nafternoon and evening hours for the next couple of days and SPC\nhas portions of the FA in a marginal risk of severe\nthunderstorms for both Day 1 and Day 2 as these systems push \nacross the area. Damaging wind gusts will be the primary severe \nthreat with these storms. A stronger northern stream shortwave \nis progged to push across the Mid-Atlantic Friday with the \nattendant cold front pushing into the area bringing the best \nforcing and chances for widespread showers and storms across the\narea. High pressure build into the area over the weekend \nbringing bringing a drier airmass and minimal chances for \nstorms.",
